messages:
Deepa: quick question — for /v2/generate (structured output) we have inconsistent behavior: some backends return `\"meta\": null` while others omit `meta` entirely. Clients are blowing up in TS. What should the contract be?

Carlos: yeah i've seen that. runtime wrappers sometimes serialize `None` -> `null` and others drop keys.

Ben: client side note: our TS types treat `meta?: { ... }` so `null` is not assignable -> runtime error when we try to access fields. simplest is to never return `null` for object fields.

Alice: strong vote for canonical rule: optional object fields should be omitted when absent. use empty object/array when intentionally present-but-empty. avoid `null` for structured types. :thumbsup:

Emma: Agreed. We have an internal guideline that said "avoid null for complex types" but it's not enforced. we should add a server-side normalizer and a lint/check in the contract tests.

Deepa: here's an example that failed for a client:```json
{
  "id": "abc",
  "results": [
    { "text": "hi", "meta": null }
  ]
}
```Client expected `results[0].meta?.source` but accessing `meta.source` threw.

Carlos: proposed runtime fix (pseudocode):```js
// normalize before send
if (typeof payload.results === 'object') {
  payload.results.forEach(r => {
    if (r.meta === null) delete r.meta;
  });
}
```This keeps payload small and consistent.

Ben: will the change be breaking for any clients that *expect* a `meta: null` sentinel? I doubt many, but worth scanning usage. I can grep for `.meta === null` in our SDK and a few big customers.

Alice: action items: 1) spec PR to document: "omit optional object fields instead of null" (Carlos) 2) runtime normalizer canary (Carlos) 3) client guards + SDK minor release to tolerate null -> treat as omitted (Ben) 4) add a contract test that fails on `null` for object fields (Emma)

Deepa: +1. Can we also handle arrays? e.g., `items: null` vs `[]` — recommended: use `[]` if present-and-empty, otherwise omit.

Carlos: yep will include arrays in the spec. will open PR shortly: https://github.com/redwood-inference/platform-specs/pull/12 (draft). putting INT-4321 on this.

deploy-bot: canary deploy scheduled: canary/runtime-normalizer v0.24 -> prod-canary at 2026-03-18T16:20Z

Ben: i'll start a quick grep + small SDK change to treat `null` as `undefined` for object fields, push branch `sdk/lenient-meta-null`.

Emma: i'll add contract test in the api-contract repo and wire it into the smoke CI. test will run against canary endpoint.

Deepa: perfect. if we can ship the canary today and monitor errors for 48h we can roll. thanks all :heart:

Alice: small nit: also add a note in changelog for backend teams so model adapters don't reintroduce `null`.

Carlos: noted — will add checklist in PR and ping model-adapters.

Ben: ping me once PR is merged, i'll cut SDK patch.

Deepa: end state: spec + canary + SDK guard + contract test. owners: Carlos (spec+runtime), Ben (SDK), Emma (tests).
